{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Starts Dating Marco"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Walk in the Park"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le09ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past & Past Continuous Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was happening at a particular time in the past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was cooking <span class=\"strong\">when</span> you texted me."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">While</span> I was swinging on the swing, it started to rain."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My pants were ripping <span class=\"strong\">as</span> I fell."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Form: subject + was/were + verb-ing</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense. </br></br> The Past Continuous talks about a longer \u2018background' action.  </br></br>The Simple Past talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words <span class=\"strong\">when, while</span> and <span class=\"strong\">as</span>."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Reacting to a Story"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When someone tells you a story, it is important to react to show that you are listening. You can show surprise and interest."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Chelsea</span>: I fell into the sand!</br> <span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: No way! What happened?"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Show Surprise\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Show Interest \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Oh?</br> Oh yeah?</br> Really?</br> Oh, really?</br> Is that right?</br> What happened?</br>  No way!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Wow!</br> No! </br>Oh boy!</br> Amazing!</br> That's unbelievable!</br> Get out of here!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "teeter totter"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a long board on which two people sit, one at each end, going up and down"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't like playing on the teeter totter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about an event that happened at the playground."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fly off"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move through the air quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I went flying off the teeter totter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to land"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to come down through the air "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I landed on the hard cement."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cut"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to break the skin and make it bleed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The glass cut my finger."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "forehead"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the part of your face above your eyes and below your hair"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I got a cut on my forehead."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stitch"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a piece of thread used to sew the edges of a wound together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I had to get 6 stitches in my head."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to injure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to hurt yourself"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I injured my knee when I kicked the ball."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lacrosse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a team sport where each player has a long stick with a net on the end of it and uses this to throw, catch, and carry a small ball"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I play lacrosse in the summer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob02aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of something that happened to you when you were a child."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell your partner the story about what happened."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to your partner's story. React to their story."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what I was doing when something else happened."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I tell a story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen and react to a story."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": 